<title>USA: Integon Corp Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Integon Corp Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>WINSTON-SALEM, N.C. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997    1996</p>
<p> Net Premiums Written			     $202,554 $194,262</p>
<p> Total Revenues					209,219  178,820</p>
<p> Operating Earnings (Loss)			 (33,075)   2,035</p>
<p>Net Realized Investment Gains (Losses)</p>
<p>  (net of taxes)					  (313)   1,350</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)				   (33,388)   3,385</p>
<p> Net Income after pfd divs			 (34,781)   1,992</p>
<p> EPS (fully diluted): Oper earnings		(2.19)     .04</p>
<p> Net Realized Investment Gains (Losses)	   (.02)     .09</p>
<p>  Net Income (Loss)				    (2.21)     .13</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares Outstanding	     15,736  15,903</p>
<p>		(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q1 1997 results include a pretax $42.0 million increase to loss reserves, or $27.3 million, or $1.73 a share, on an after-tax basis. It also includes the related write off of deferred policy acquisition costs of pretax $3.7 million, or $2.4 million, or $0.15 per share, on an after-tax basis.</p>
<p>Q1 1997 EPS excluding those two items and the net realized investment gains/losses would have been a loss of $0.31 a share.</p>
</text>
